<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ebussuud Efendi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1490">1490</a>–<a href="/years/1574">1574</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Mehmed Ebüssuûd Efendi, El-İmâdî</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ebussuud Efendi was an Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanafi-school">Hanafi</a> jurist and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quran">Quran</a> exegete who served as qadi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a> from 1533 to 1537 and as Shaykh al-Islām, the empire's supreme judge, from 1545 until his death. Working closely with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a>, he built a legal framework joining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharia">sharia</a> with the sultan's administrative law (qānūn), under which judges derived their power from the sultan and had to follow his law-letters. He systematised the issuing of fatwās and wrote thousands of them: some legitimised Suleiman's killings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazidis">Yazidis</a> and declared the killing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qizilbash">Qizilbash</a> praiseworthy, others allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a> and Karagöz plays. He completed a commentary on the whole Quran in 1566.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>Ebussuud Efendi</b>, şeyhülislam from 1545 to 1574, worked with Suleiman the Magnificent to reconcile the sultan’s law (kanun) with the sharia, and issued thousands of legal opinions (fatwas), on matters from land tenure to the drinking of coffee.</blockquote><a href="/societies/ottoman-empire">Social Hierarchy of the Ottoman Empire</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in İskilip, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istanbul">Istanbul</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.73,34.47&amp;year=1544" aria-label="İskilip on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5395 709 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Ebussuud Efendi"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5845 979h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5845 979h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=40.73,34.47&amp;year=1544">What was here in 1544? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
